*> The block atlas (texture 0; 08 §7.2, §7.3, §10.2; research R4): ATLAS-BUILD runs the sources of
*> the block and item atlas definitions of every pack (definitions merge across packs, bottom pack
*> first; "directory" lists textures/<source>/... in every namespace of every pack, "single" adds
*> one texture; a later add with the same sprite id replaces the earlier), reads each sprite from
*> the top-most pack that has it and stitches the sprites in rows into an atlas 128 pixels wide.
*> Sprite 1 is the missing-texture stripes (standin-content §1.4.2), generated by MISSING-TEXTURE,
*> not a pack file. ATLAS-FIND looks a sprite id up (0 = unresolved: callers use sprite 1);
*> ATLAS-UV maps sprite units to atlas texture coordinates.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. ATLAS-BUILD.
*> USING CLIENT-STATE: fills AT-* and marks texture 0 for upload.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLCONST.
 COPY JSONDOC.
 01 WS-DEFS.
    05 FILLER PIC X(40) VALUE "assets/minecraft/atlases/blocks.json".
    05 FILLER PIC X(40) VALUE "assets/minecraft/atlases/items.json".
 01 WS-DEF-TABLE REDEFINES WS-DEFS.
    05 WS-DEF              PIC X(40) OCCURS 2 TIMES.
 01 WS-D                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-P                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-Q                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-S                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-FOUND               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SOURCE              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-FIELD               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SOURCES             BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-PATH                PIC X(256).
 01 WS-PATH-LENGTH         BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-FILE                PIC X(256).
 01 WS-FILE-LENGTH         BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TEXT                PIC X(65536).
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 65536.
 01 WS-LENGTH              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-NAME                PIC X(16).
 01 WS-NAME-LENGTH         BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TYPE                PIC X(32).
 01 WS-DIR                 PIC X(128).
 01 WS-DIR-LENGTH          BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-PREFIX              PIC X(128).
 01 WS-PREFIX-LENGTH       BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-VALUE-CAP           BINARY-LONG VALUE 128.
 01 WS-TYPE-LENGTH         BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-NS                  PIC X(64).
 01 WS-NS-LENGTH           BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-REST                PIC X(128).
 01 WS-REST-LENGTH         BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ID                  PIC X(80).
 01 WS-ID-LENGTH           BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SPRITE-PATH         PIC X(256) OCCURS 128 TIMES.
 01 WS-SPRITE-PATH-LENGTH  BINARY-LONG OCCURS 128 TIMES.
 01 WS-IMAGE               PIC X(1048576).
 01 WS-IMAGE-CAP           BINARY-LONG VALUE 1048576.
 01 WS-W                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-H                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-X                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-Y                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ROW-H               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-BYTES               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SIXTEEN             BINARY-LONG VALUE 16.
 01 WS-SIXTEEN2            BINARY-LONG VALUE 16.
 01 B-ATLAS                PIC X(1073741824) BASED.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CLIENT-STATE.
     MOVE 1 TO AT-SPRITE-COUNT
     INITIALIZE AT-SPRITE(1)
     MOVE "missing" TO AT-NAME(1)
     MOVE 7 TO AT-NAME-LENGTH(1)
     MOVE 16 TO AT-SW(1) AT-SH(1)
     PERFORM VARYING WS-D FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-D > 2
         MOVE WS-DEF(WS-D) TO WS-FILE
         MOVE FUNCTION LENGTH(FUNCTION TRIM(WS-FILE)) TO WS-FILE-LENGTH
         PERFORM VARYING WS-P FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-P > PK-COUNT
             CALL "PACK-SOURCE-HAS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-P WS-FILE WS-FILE-LENGTH WS-FOUND
             MOVE 0 TO WS-SOURCE
             IF WS-FOUND = 1
                 CALL "PACK-SOURCE-READ" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-P WS-FILE WS-FILE-LENGTH WS-TEXT
                     WS-CAPACITY WS-LENGTH WS-FOUND
                 CALL "JSON-PARSE" USING JSON-DOC WS-TEXT WS-LENGTH
                 MOVE "sources" TO WS-NAME
                 MOVE 7 TO WS-NAME-LENGTH
                 MOVE 1 TO WS-I
                 CALL "JSON-MEMBER" USING JSON-DOC WS-I WS-NAME WS-NAME-LENGTH WS-SOURCES
                 IF WS-SOURCES > 0
                     MOVE JN-FIRST(WS-SOURCES) TO WS-SOURCE
                 END-IF
             END-IF
             PERFORM UNTIL WS-SOURCE = 0
                 MOVE SPACES TO WS-TYPE WS-DIR WS-PREFIX
                 MOVE "type" TO WS-NAME
                 MOVE 4 TO WS-NAME-LENGTH
                 CALL "JSON-MEMBER" USING JSON-DOC WS-SOURCE WS-NAME WS-NAME-LENGTH WS-FIELD
                 CALL "JSON-STRING" USING JSON-DOC WS-FIELD WS-TYPE WS-VALUE-CAP WS-TYPE-LENGTH
                 EVALUATE WS-TYPE
                     WHEN "directory"
                     WHEN "minecraft:directory"
*>                       Every textures/<source>/<rest>.png of every namespace of every pack
*>                       becomes sprite <namespace>:<prefix><rest>.
                         MOVE "source" TO WS-NAME
                         MOVE 6 TO WS-NAME-LENGTH
                         CALL "JSON-MEMBER" USING JSON-DOC WS-SOURCE WS-NAME WS-NAME-LENGTH
                             WS-FIELD
                         CALL "JSON-STRING" USING JSON-DOC WS-FIELD WS-DIR WS-VALUE-CAP
                             WS-DIR-LENGTH
                         MOVE "prefix" TO WS-NAME
                         CALL "JSON-MEMBER" USING JSON-DOC WS-SOURCE WS-NAME WS-NAME-LENGTH
                             WS-FIELD
                         CALL "JSON-STRING" USING JSON-DOC WS-FIELD WS-PREFIX WS-VALUE-CAP
                             WS-PREFIX-LENGTH
                         PERFORM VARYING WS-Q FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-Q > PK-COUNT
                             MOVE 1 TO WS-FOUND
                             PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-FOUND = 0
                                 CALL "PACK-SOURCE-PATH" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-Q WS-I WS-PATH
                                     WS-PATH-LENGTH WS-FOUND
                                 CALL "ATLAS-DIRECTORY-MATCH" USING WS-PATH WS-PATH-LENGTH
                                     WS-DIR WS-DIR-LENGTH WS-NS WS-NS-LENGTH WS-REST
                                     WS-REST-LENGTH
                                 IF WS-FOUND = 1 AND WS-NS-LENGTH > 0
                                     MOVE SPACES TO WS-ID
                                     STRING WS-NS(1:WS-NS-LENGTH) ":"
                                         WS-PREFIX(1:WS-PREFIX-LENGTH) WS-REST(1:WS-REST-LENGTH)
                                         DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-ID
                                     COMPUTE WS-ID-LENGTH = WS-NS-LENGTH + 1 + WS-PREFIX-LENGTH
                                         + WS-REST-LENGTH
                                     CALL "ATLAS-FIND" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-ID-LENGTH
                                         WS-S
                                     IF WS-S = 0 AND AT-SPRITE-COUNT < CL-MAX-SPRITES
                                         ADD 1 TO AT-SPRITE-COUNT
                                         MOVE AT-SPRITE-COUNT TO WS-S
                                     END-IF
                                     IF WS-S > 0
                                         INITIALIZE AT-SPRITE(WS-S)
                                         MOVE WS-ID TO AT-NAME(WS-S)
                                         MOVE WS-ID-LENGTH TO AT-NAME-LENGTH(WS-S)
                                         MOVE WS-PATH TO WS-SPRITE-PATH(WS-S)
                                         MOVE WS-PATH-LENGTH TO WS-SPRITE-PATH-LENGTH(WS-S)
                                     END-IF
                                 END-IF
                             END-PERFORM
                         END-PERFORM
                 END-EVALUATE
                 MOVE JN-NEXT(WS-SOURCE) TO WS-SOURCE
             END-PERFORM
         END-PERFORM
     END-PERFORM
*>   Sizes, then rows of sprites in order, 128 pixels wide (wider when a sprite is).
     MOVE 128 TO AT-W
     PERFORM VARYING WS-S FROM 2 BY 1 UNTIL WS-S > AT-SPRITE-COUNT
         CALL "PACK-IMAGE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-SPRITE-PATH(WS-S) WS-SPRITE-PATH-LENGTH(WS-S)
             WS-IMAGE WS-IMAGE-CAP AT-SW(WS-S) AT-SH(WS-S) WS-FOUND
*>       A texture that cannot be decoded is drawn as the missing texture (US18-5).
         IF WS-FOUND = 0
             MOVE 16 TO AT-SW(WS-S) AT-SH(WS-S)
         END-IF
         MOVE FUNCTION MAX(AT-W, AT-SW(WS-S)) TO AT-W
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE 0 TO WS-X WS-Y WS-ROW-H
     PERFORM VARYING WS-S FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-S > AT-SPRITE-COUNT
         IF WS-X + AT-SW(WS-S) > AT-W
             ADD WS-ROW-H TO WS-Y
             MOVE 0 TO WS-X WS-ROW-H
         END-IF
         MOVE WS-X TO AT-X(WS-S)
         MOVE WS-Y TO AT-Y(WS-S)
         ADD AT-SW(WS-S) TO WS-X
         MOVE FUNCTION MAX(WS-ROW-H, AT-SH(WS-S)) TO WS-ROW-H
     END-PERFORM
     COMPUTE AT-H = WS-Y + WS-ROW-H
     IF AT-ADDR NOT = NULL
         FREE AT-ADDR
     END-IF
     COMPUTE WS-BYTES = AT-W * AT-H * 4
     ALLOCATE WS-BYTES CHARACTERS INITIALIZED RETURNING AT-ADDR
     SET ADDRESS OF B-ATLAS TO AT-ADDR
     CALL "MISSING-TEXTURE" USING WS-SIXTEEN WS-SIXTEEN2 WS-IMAGE
     PERFORM VARYING WS-S FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-S > AT-SPRITE-COUNT
         IF WS-S > 1
             CALL "PACK-IMAGE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-SPRITE-PATH(WS-S)
                 WS-SPRITE-PATH-LENGTH(WS-S) WS-IMAGE WS-IMAGE-CAP WS-W WS-H WS-FOUND
             IF WS-FOUND = 0
                 CALL "MISSING-TEXTURE" USING WS-SIXTEEN WS-SIXTEEN2 WS-IMAGE
             END-IF
         END-IF
         PERFORM VARYING WS-Y FROM 0 BY 1 UNTIL WS-Y >= AT-SH(WS-S)
             COMPUTE WS-I = ((AT-Y(WS-S) + WS-Y) * AT-W + AT-X(WS-S)) * 4 + 1
             MOVE WS-IMAGE(WS-Y * AT-SW(WS-S) * 4 + 1:AT-SW(WS-S) * 4)
                 TO B-ATLAS(WS-I:AT-SW(WS-S) * 4)
         END-PERFORM
*>       Translucent when any pixel has alpha below 255 (08 §5.3).
         PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 4 BY 4 UNTIL WS-I > AT-SW(WS-S) * AT-SH(WS-S) * 4
             IF WS-IMAGE(WS-I:1) NOT = X"FF"
                 MOVE 1 TO AT-TRANSLUCENT(WS-S)
             END-IF
         END-PERFORM
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE 1 TO AT-UPLOAD(1)
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM ATLAS-BUILD.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. ATLAS-DIRECTORY-MATCH.
*> USING path (PIC X(256)), path length, source directory (PIC X(128)), its length, namespace out
*> (PIC X(64)), namespace length out (0 = no match), rest out (PIC X(128)), rest length out: a path
*> assets/<namespace>/textures/<source>/<rest>.png gives the namespace and the rest.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 01 WS-SLASH               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-HEAD                PIC X(256).
 01 WS-HEAD-LENGTH         BINARY-LONG.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-PATH                 PIC X(256).
 01 L-LENGTH               BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-DIR                  PIC X(128).
 01 L-DIR-LENGTH           BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-NS                   PIC X(64).
 01 L-NS-LENGTH            BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-REST                 PIC X(128).
 01 L-REST-LENGTH          BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-PATH L-LENGTH L-DIR L-DIR-LENGTH L-NS L-NS-LENGTH L-REST
         L-REST-LENGTH.
     MOVE 0 TO L-NS-LENGTH WS-SLASH
     IF L-PATH(1:7) = "assets/" AND L-PATH(L-LENGTH - 3:4) = ".png" AND L-LENGTH > 11
         INSPECT L-PATH(8:L-LENGTH - 7) TALLYING WS-SLASH FOR CHARACTERS BEFORE INITIAL "/"
         MOVE SPACES TO WS-HEAD
         STRING "/textures/" L-DIR(1:L-DIR-LENGTH) "/" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-HEAD
         COMPUTE WS-HEAD-LENGTH = L-DIR-LENGTH + 11
         IF L-PATH(8 + WS-SLASH:WS-HEAD-LENGTH) = WS-HEAD(1:WS-HEAD-LENGTH)
             MOVE WS-SLASH TO L-NS-LENGTH
             MOVE L-PATH(8:WS-SLASH) TO L-NS
             COMPUTE L-REST-LENGTH = L-LENGTH - 7 - WS-SLASH - WS-HEAD-LENGTH - 4
             MOVE L-PATH(8 + WS-SLASH + WS-HEAD-LENGTH:L-REST-LENGTH) TO L-REST
         END-IF
     END-IF
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM ATLAS-DIRECTORY-MATCH.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. ATLAS-FIND.
*> USING CLIENT-STATE, sprite id (PIC X(80)), id length, sprite out (0 when unresolved).
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 01 WS-S                   BINARY-LONG.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 01 L-ID                   PIC X(80).
 01 L-LENGTH               BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-SPRITE               BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CLIENT-STATE L-ID L-LENGTH L-SPRITE.
     MOVE 0 TO L-SPRITE
     PERFORM VARYING WS-S FROM 2 BY 1 UNTIL WS-S > AT-SPRITE-COUNT OR L-SPRITE > 0
         IF AT-NAME-LENGTH(WS-S) = L-LENGTH AND AT-NAME(WS-S) = L-ID
             MOVE WS-S TO L-SPRITE
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM ATLAS-FIND.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. ATLAS-UV.
*> USING CLIENT-STATE, sprite, u and v in sprite units 0 to 16 (FLOAT-SHORT), u and v out: atlas
*> texture coordinates 0 to 1.
 DATA DIVISION.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 01 L-SPRITE               BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-U16                  FLOAT-SHORT.
 01 L-V16                  FLOAT-SHORT.
 01 L-U                    FLOAT-SHORT.
 01 L-V                    FLOAT-SHORT.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CLIENT-STATE L-SPRITE L-U16 L-V16 L-U L-V.
     COMPUTE L-U = (AT-X(L-SPRITE) + L-U16 * AT-SW(L-SPRITE) / 16) / AT-W
     COMPUTE L-V = (AT-Y(L-SPRITE) + L-V16 * AT-SH(L-SPRITE) / 16) / AT-H
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM ATLAS-UV.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. MISSING-TEXTURE.
*> USING width, height, RGBA out (width x height x 4 bytes): standin-content §1.4.2 missing texture:
*> #F28C28 where ((x + y) div 2) mod 2 = 0, otherwise #1A1A1A.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 01 WS-X                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-Y                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-D                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ORANGE              PIC X(4).
 01 WS-DARK                PIC X(4).
 01 B-RGBA                 PIC X(1073741824) BASED.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-W                    BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-H                    BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-RGBA                 PIC X.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-W L-H L-RGBA.
     SET ADDRESS OF B-RGBA TO ADDRESS OF L-RGBA
     MOVE FUNCTION HEX-TO-CHAR("F28C28FF") TO WS-ORANGE
     MOVE FUNCTION HEX-TO-CHAR("1A1A1AFF") TO WS-DARK
     PERFORM VARYING WS-Y FROM 0 BY 1 UNTIL WS-Y >= L-H
         PERFORM VARYING WS-X FROM 0 BY 1 UNTIL WS-X >= L-W
             COMPUTE WS-D = WS-X + WS-Y
             DIVIDE WS-D BY 2 GIVING WS-D
             IF FUNCTION MOD(WS-D, 2) = 0
                 MOVE WS-ORANGE TO B-RGBA((WS-Y * L-W + WS-X) * 4 + 1:4)
             ELSE
                 MOVE WS-DARK TO B-RGBA((WS-Y * L-W + WS-X) * 4 + 1:4)
             END-IF
         END-PERFORM
     END-PERFORM
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM MISSING-TEXTURE.
